rem Summation of a Modular Formula
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=717

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Limit integer = 10 ** 7

rem By Fermat, b = 2^(2^p) mod p is
rem 2^(2^p mod (p-1)) mod p. Halving
rem mod p gives h with 2h = b; then
rem w = h 2^p mod p^2 equals b + p g
rem with g the wanted residue.
Sieve = (Limit - 1) primesieve
Primes = (Sieve array) drop 1
Reduced = 2 Primes (Primes - 1) powmod
Power = 2 Reduced Primes powmod
Inverse2 = (Primes + 1) // 2
Half = Power * Inverse2 mod Primes
Squares = Primes * Primes
TwoPow = 2 Primes Squares powmod
Lift = Half * TwoPow mod Squares
Diff = (Lift - Power) mod Squares
Digits = Diff // Primes
return Digits sum
